---
import DocsLayout from '../../DocsLayout.astro';
import { shortcutGroups } from '../../../bureau/shortcuts';
const groups = shortcutGroups('en');
---
<DocsLayout lang="en" id="clavier" description="Every keyboard shortcut of the Bureau, and what makes it usable without a mouse and with a screen reader.">
  <p class="prose__lead">Everything the mouse does can be done with the keyboard. In the Bureau, <kbd>?</kbd> shows this list.</p>

  {groups.map((g) => (
    <section>
      <h2>{g.title}</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          {g.rows.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{r.keys.map((k) => <kbd>{k}</kbd>)}</th>
              <td>{r.what}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The desk is a list of items you move through with the arrows; each paper announces its title, type and state. Moves, selection, zoom and undo are announced.</li>
    <li>“Vue liste” shows the same files in an ordinary list, with the same selection.</li>
    <li>Each tool says its name, shortcut and what it does; an unavailable tool stays reachable and says why.</li>
    <li>Selection and focus outlines stay visible in high-contrast mode; the system’s “reduce motion” turns animations off.</li>
    <li>Light or dark theme: menu, “Display”, or the system’s.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
